+# High-value unknowns
+
+Canonical list after Mission 1 / 1.5. Not a literature search. Not group-final.
+
+Each item is tagged. None of these is filled by Hu’s 1.8 nM AuED-MEA Langmuir–Freundlich apparent Kd, by missing `koff`, or by overnight T1.
+
+## 1. Is 1.8 nM affinity or interface/transduction?
+
+**Unknown.** Paired solution-phase and surface Kd of Hu’s exact Fc-thiol 39-mer, same buffer, Langmuir and Langmuir–Freundlich, exponent *n*, achieved coverage.
+
+**Why it matters.** Decides whether confinement is a measured result, whether the 1:1 81-fold window may be drawn on this sensor, and what θ at any chosen concentration would even be. The retinal PaC probe still would not inherit that number without its own isotherm.
+
+Tag: `proposed experiment`
+
+## 2. Is the retina ACV chemically glutamate?
+
+**Unknown.** TTX, CNQX/AP5, TBOA, plus a scrambled-aptamer probe on the same shank.
+
+**Why it matters.** S066 Probes 1–2 are light-correlated ACV, not a pharmacological identification. Without this, “the device already works at basal” remains a correlation.
+
+Tag: `proposed experiment`
+
+## 3. Glutamate aptamer kon / koff on the 39-mer
+
+**Unknown.** IPA or SPR under controlled mass transport. C007 is an empty cell in the inspected set. C008/C010 are not glutamate.
+
+**Why it matters.** Converts the transient column from untested to tested. τ_eq = 1/(kon *c* + koff) cannot be computed from a glutamate measurement today. Missing koff does not prove slow kinetics.
+
+Tag: `unresolved` / `proposed experiment`
+
+## 4. Glu versus Asp / Gln / GABA in PBS and Ames
+
+**Unknown.** Signal-gain ratios on the same oligo at interferent-realistic concentrations. C032: thesis panel is 100 nM Glu vs 10 µM serotonin, dopamine, tyrosine, lactate. Asp/Gln/GABA absent. Public Ames L-glutamine arithmetic is not a ledger interference result (vendor identity unresolved).
+
+**Why it matters.** Decides whether the tissue signal can be the analyte. Not a fifth title (W1 REJECT).
+
+Tag: `unresolved`
+
+## 5. Probe 3: occupancy versus lost gold
+
+**Unknown.** Paired electroactive surface area, 1 kHz impedance, and aptamer coverage before/after insertion, alongside the light test. Fig. 6.16 already shows gold-nanostructure detachment.
+
+**Why it matters.** The only in-tissue “early saturation” sentence is gold-confounded. Probes 1–2 still modulate.
+
+Tag: `unresolved`
+
+## Related unknowns (do not displace the five)
+
+- PaC-probe apparent Kd in Ames/tissue (empty). Distinct from unknown 1 if that pair is measured on AuED-MEA rather than the shank.
+- GCL/IPL-border electrode versus photoreceptor-terminal narrative.
+- In vivo glutamate aptamer sensor (C020). S066 is in vitro mouse retina.
+- Wu 2022 VoR (1d04/glu1 beyond the abstract).
+- Clements VoR (1.1 mM / 1.2 ms remain abstract inference).
+- Abrantes millimolar ELONA Kd (not entered; API tokens `10.3` / `25.1` are funder IDs).
+
+## What would most change the current thesis
+
+Recorded in `reports/mission1_story_tournament.md` §7 and `state/current_thesis.md` (falsifier). Highest-information single experiment remains unknown 1, or unknown 2 if the poster’s question is retina biology. Do not do both and report neither.
