+# Opus 5 blind story-gate closure review
+
+Agent: `bc-7da27ff4-88b3-5acc-b4cc-ad86a0beaa66`
+Model: `claude-opus-5-thinking-xhigh`
+Blind: asked only whether named revisions resolve the reasons the gate previously failed. No desired PASS outcome was given. Packet: `rounds/mission1_closure/packet.md`.
+
+Saved verbatim from the reviewer output.
+
+---
+
+## Method
+
+I read, in this order: `rounds/mission1_closure/packet.md`; `.cursor/rules/safety-and-integrity.mdc` (it exists, is hash-locked, and I read it in full — the previous reviewer's report that it was absent is recorded as an orchestrator correction in both the prior review and the Mission 1 report, and nothing in it contradicts the prior verdict); `.cursor/rules/research-constitution.mdc`; `.cursor/rules/scoring-rubric.mdc`; `state/current_thesis.md`; `poster/storyboards/revised_D.md`; `research/reviews/premium/opus_story_gate.md`; `reports/mission1_story_tournament.md` (including §13); `state/claims.csv`; `research/evidence/core_evidence.csv`; `research/evidence/poster_numbers.md`; `research/evidence/quantity_ontology.md`; `research/reviews/contradictions.md`; `research/reviews/citation_audit.md`; `state/model_disagreements.md`; `state/high_value_unknowns.md`; `analysis/accepted/occupancy_kinetics/figures/CAPTION.md`; `analysis/accepted/occupancy_kinetics/limitations.md`; `state/gates/science_story.json`; and the raw XML of `analysis/accepted/figures/span_identity.svg`, `two_regime_clocks.svg`, and `occupancy.svg`.
+
+I opened nothing outside the MAY-read list. I did not read `reports/nightly_summary.md`, `poster/theses.md`, `poster/storyboards/winner.md`, `analysis/candidates/theses/`, `rounds/03/`, or `state/scoreboard.json`. One directory listing of `analysis/accepted/` exposed the filenames `atlas.svg`, `clocks.svg`, `sensitivity.svg`, `figures.py`, and `tests/`; I opened none of them. Consequence to declare up front: **Panel 5's glyph (`atlas.svg`) is un-inspected in this review**, so I certify Panel 5 only from the storyboard text and the ledger, and I did not read the figure generator or its tests, so my check on the flagship computation is an independent one rather than a code review.
+
+Because I could not read the generator, I verified the flagship figure by arithmetic on its own SVG coordinates. `span_identity.svg` places its plot from x=70 to x=750 over a stated 9-decade axis (10 pM to 10 mM), i.e. 75.556 px/decade. The Herman tick sits at x=326.73, which is 25 nM to four figures; the Clements tick sits at x=677.57, which is 1.1 mM; the ratio drawn between them is 44,000-fold exactly, as labeled. The MODELED band runs x=375.68 to x=519.88, a width of 144.20 px = 1.9085 decades = 81.0-fold, and its left edge corresponds to 111 nM, i.e. it is anchored at c₁₀ = Kd/9 for a generic Kd of 1 µM, as the figure's own footer states. The band therefore encloses neither the Herman tick (left of it) nor the Clements tick (right of it), which is the argument in visual form. I also confirmed by scanning every drawn element's coordinates that **no glyph exists at the 1.8 nM position (x≈240) in the flagship**. The two arithmetic claims the thesis leans on — 81-fold from c₉₀/c₁₀ = 9Kd/(Kd/9), and 44,000-fold from 1.1 mM / 25 nM — are exact, and θ(25 nM) on a 1:1 Kd of 1.8 nM is 0.933, matching the 0.93 the thesis disowns.
+
+## Direct answer to the question
+
+**Yes. The named revisions resolve the reasons this gate previously failed.** The prior REVISE rested on five specific defects: the occupancy half of Candidate D was not primary (a 1:1 overlay of a Langmuir–Freundlich EC50 measured on a different device); Probe 3 was used as a saturation observation when the thesis attributes it to detached gold; the H2/H3 GCL-IPL layer tension was unaddressed; the θ=0.93 curve was the load-bearing glyph; and the D-over-C margin was partly earned by the half that was then withdrawn. Each is now repaired in the canonical artifacts rather than only in prose: `state/current_thesis.md` withdraws occupancy-as-finding and stamps PaC occupancy unmeasured, `poster/storyboards/revised_D.md` makes Panel 4's claim the UNKNOWN itself and demotes `occupancy.svg`, the flagship `span_identity.svg` does not draw 1.8 nM at all, the gold-detachment confound and the electrode-layer tension are both printed on-panel, and the cleft column is restated as untested rather than failed.
+
+The repair is not cosmetic and it is not a relabeling of the old claim. What survives is also a weaker claim than the one submitted, and the package says so in its own Historical note. What I do find are four load-bearing facts that the revision imported to satisfy the earlier objections and did not promote into `state/claims.csv` or `research/evidence/core_evidence.csv`, plus three production-grade labeling defects and one test name that still asserts the withdrawn finding. None of these reinstates the withdrawn claim and none requires a change to the thesis or to the flagship figures' content.
+
+## Criterion 1 — One thesis materially stronger than the other three: **PASS**
+
+The reason this bullet was recorded as "Partial" was not a tie; it was that the 85 was earned in part by scoring occupancy as demonstrated and then withdrawing it in the gate list, which the adversarial reading correctly called internally inconsistent. The right test now is what remains after the withdrawal, and whether that remainder still beats A, B and C as a title.
+
+It does, and on the locked rubric rather than on a re-score. Revised D's surviving load-bearing content is Herman's own two-component framing with ambient near 25 nM in acute hippocampal slice (C012/E034, full text inspected), the exact 81-fold 1:1 identity that admits no aptamer number at all (C027 as algebra, C013 as a community statement of the same identity), the ~44,000-fold arithmetic on two labeled literature examples, the S066 clocks and the authors' own basal-not-transient sentence (C028/C031/E042/E045/E046, inspected), the light-correlated ACV on Probes 1–2 as positive evidence inside that regime, and an honestly empty glutamate kon/koff cell (C007). That is still a claim about the world — neurochemistry presents two measurement regimes and the only nervous-tissue experiment in this ledger occupies one of them — whereas A remains a definition that cannot be wrong, B restates a caveat Hu himself wrote in §3.2 and carries its own counterexample inside the same Langmuir–Freundlich panel, and C's strong form is false against Hu's 32 pM, leaving working-range arithmetic that is a panel.
+
+Two honest qualifications that do not change the grade. First, no post-revision tournament score exists; the only number is a synthesizer's 89, which the repository itself disclaims as not a second independent pass, and I am not supplying a substitute score because the criterion asks about material strength, not about re-ranking. Second, A, B and C have been converted into supporting panels of D with their titles retired, so "stronger than the other three" is now partly a statement about absorption rather than defeat. I checked the comparison on its merits anyway and the margin holds on central-question relevance, which is where it always lived: after revision D is the only one of the four that states a testable match-or-mismatch between a biological quantity and a chemical one.
+
+## Criterion 2 — Load-bearing claims have primary evidence: **PASS**
+
+This was the hard "no", and the two stated reasons are gone. The occupancy assertion is withdrawn rather than re-worded: the thesis states the PaC probe has no reported apparent Kd in Ames or tissue, types Hu's 1.8 nM as C005's AuED-MEA Langmuir–Freundlich `EC50` in PBS on a different device with a different isotherm class, and marks the 1:1 overlay a `computational illustration` of advertised numbers. Probe 3 is no longer evidence of saturation; it is author-flagged failure analysis with the occupancy reading `unresolved`, matching Fig. 6.16 and C's earlier honesty. The cleft column no longer rests on the 1992 inference as though it were a retinal measurement: C011 is labeled abstract-only, a kinetic inference rather than a chemical assay, at cultured hippocampal synapses, with transfer to retina `unknown`. That is the correct repair for an abstract-only source whose version of record is closed — lower the assertion to what the abstract supports rather than upgrade the source, and record `full_text_inspected=no`, which the ledger does.
+
+I walked the ten load-bearing rows against the ledger. Rows 1, 4, 7 and 10 are inspected primary (E034; E042/E045/E046 plus C006; S066 Fig. 6.16; C032 as an intentionally empty panel). Row 2 is correctly graded as algebra plus a review statement of the same identity, and it is an identity, so primary empirical evidence is not the applicable demand. Row 3 is primary as those papers' own results with transfer marked unknown. Row 6 is the empty cell, correctly `unresolved`, with C005 retained as primary evidence about a *different* device. Row 8 is an absence plus a `computational illustration`, and it declines the cheap kill — τ_eq = 1/(kon·c + koff) can be short at millimolar c even when t_off is long, so missing koff is not evidence of slow kinetics.
+
+The defect is in rows 5 and 9, the two rows the revision added to answer the earlier objections. Row 5 — Probes 1–2 produced light-correlated ACV in the direction expected for basal glutamate — is stamped MEASURED on Panel 3 and cited to C031 and S066, but neither C031 nor any other `claims.csv` row asserts that outcome; C031 records the clocks and the authors' basal-not-transient sentence. The experiment itself *is* in the ledger with a locator and an inspection flag (E046, "section 6.3; Fig. 6.13", `full_text_inspected=yes`), and its notes carry only the Probe 3 and Probe 4 outcomes, so the claim is traceable today but not stated. Row 9 — the electrode reported at the GCL/IPL border against a photoreceptor-terminal mechanism sentence — has no ledger row at all and is cited to "S066; H2/H3", i.e. partly to sealed lane notes. I grade this PASS rather than REVISE because the underlying primary evidence exists at a named locator in an inspected row, the closed ten-type quantity vocabulary has no slot for "light-correlated ACV" so an empty-value row in the style of C032 is the correct vehicle, and because row 9 is used to *withhold* a claim (UNKNOWN which pool) rather than to assert one. But the storyboard defines MEASURED as "inspected primary result on the named construct, matrix, and device", and a MEASURED stamp with no claim row is not traceable by a student at the panel. Both rows must be promoted with tag, locator and `full_text_inspected` before anything is printed.
+
+## Criterion 3 — Survives the counterevidence in its own dossier and `contradictions.md`: **PASS**
+
+Both named unaddressed items are now explicit. The Fig. 6.16 gold-nanostructure detachment is in the thesis body, in load-bearing row 7, in Panel 4, and in the Probe 3 row of `state/model_disagreements.md`, with the occupancy reading left `unresolved` and the observation that detachment can mimic early saturation. The layer tension is in row 9, in Panel 3's instruction to print it on-panel, and on the canvas of `two_regime_clocks.svg` as "GCL/IPL electrode vs photoreceptor narrative: UNKNOWN pool". Neither is resolved, which is correct; both are displayed.
+
+The rest of `contradictions.md` is handled. §2's empty kinetics is row 8, with the tobramycin IPA and Ding ITC envelopes explicitly non-transferable and the 2 ms interrogation clock kept distinct from koff. §5's Park glutamate-dehydrogenase mislabel is not harvested. §6's in-vivo leap is refused in both the Inference boundary and the Must-not-claim list. §7's docking failure is not used. The corrected Ames glutamine arithmetic survives as `unresolved` with the fold stated as 50× at the Ames ceiling rather than the earlier 10⁵, which is a real arithmetic correction properly recorded rather than quietly dropped. The H2-versus-C031 dispute stays live in `model_disagreements.md` with the canonical position that S066 is simultaneously the strongest nervous-tissue experiment here and a device-level feasibility result rather than a chemical identification — and the thesis uses exactly that wording.
+
+One counterevidence item is survived but not displayed where it matters. The sharpest objection to the newly elevated positive claim is the authors' own statement that the Ames calibration carries 41.6% blank noise and poor quantitative SNR (C030/E044). Panel 3 stamps UNKNOWN for absolute [Glu], and Panel 5 carries the Ames-versus-PBS split, so the claim as stated does survive — no absolute concentration is asserted, and the Ames SNR is precisely why. But the panel that makes the positive claim should print the authors' caveat next to it rather than leaving it two panels away, and the 41.6% figure appears nowhere in the thesis or storyboard text.
+
+## Criterion 4 — Fits one poster a first-year can draw without collapsing Kd/LOD/EC50/clocks: **PASS**
+
+The prior grade was "yes, conditionally", and the condition was that quantity type and device move out of captions and onto the panel. That condition is substantially met. `span_identity.svg` names the isotherm class, the device and the matrix in on-canvas body text and labels each concentration tick by preparation ("acute hippocampal slice — not retina"; "cultured hippocampal synapses — different prep"). `two_regime_clocks.svg` carries all of its content on canvas with 16 px bold stamps. Even the demoted `occupancy.svg` now carries the device inside the legend entry itself — "AuED-MEA LF 1.8 nM (not PaC)" — plus "PaC θ UNKNOWN" inside the plot area, which is the substance of what was asked. The six-panel structure is drawable: two labeled wells, a sliding band against two ticks, two columns of clocks, an empty well, a table, and a protocol cartoon.
+
+On collapse: the families stay apart. `Kd_molecular` (1d04 12 µM; Xiao SPR 293 nM) is separated from apparent electrochemical `EC50` (Hu 1.8 nM) and from receptor EC50 (Herman 1.8 µM on nucleated patches), and the digit collision across a thousandfold is named with the instruction that unit and quantity type ride in the axis label. `sensor_LOD` values stay on their own rows with estimator and matrix. The 81-fold identity is explicitly *not* filed as this device's `analytical_working_range`. `two_regime_clocks.svg` is the honest two-clock form the prior review asked for and has no shared axis to merge clock types on; each line names its own operation (14 s scan, ~1 min sampling, ~10 min plateau).
+
+Three defects remain, all fixable without touching the argument. First, Panel 5 — the panel whose entire job is number-distinctness — lists "10 fM" twice and omits Wu's 0.0013 pM glu1 LOD even though C002 appears in its own ID list. Second, `occupancy.svg` has a genuine label collision: the Clements annotation is anchored 150 px to the left of its own tick (x=372 against a line at x=522) and overlaps the Herman annotation at the same y, so at panel scale a viewer can attach the wrong preparation to the wrong tick. Third, neither flagship figure has a drawn, tick-marked axis; `span_identity.svg` states its axis only in a 12 px footer line and `occupancy.svg` carries no axis annotation at all, so "quantity type and device in the axis label" is satisfied on-canvas but not literally at the axis.
+
+## Criterion 5 — Computation answers the thesis rather than decorating it: **PASS**
+
+The flagship is now the computation that *is* the argument, and I verified it independently rather than taking the caption's word: the 81-fold band is drawn to the pixel at c₁₀ and c₉₀ of a generic 1 µM Kd, the two literature ticks land exactly on 25 nM and 1.1 mM, the bracket between them is exactly 44,000-fold, and the band's placement at a generic Kd means the ruler cannot be read as a fitted window for any real device. The figure's own footer says that is why 1 µM was chosen. The identity requires no aptamer number, which is exactly what makes it survivable, and the Langmuir–Freundlich objection is answered rather than ignored: the thesis and Panel 2 both state that Hu fitted a Langmuir–Freundlich isotherm with an unpublished heterogeneity exponent, so this sensor's 10–90% window would be 81^(1/n), and the 81-fold figure is a design principle rather than a fitted range.
+
+The decorative part is demoted, and the demotion is real: the flagship omits 1.8 nM entirely, `occupancy.svg` is titled DEMOTED on its own canvas, and the storyboard forbids it as the flagship glyph and permits it only as a captioned MODELED inset. The prior review offered two acceptable fates for the θ overlay — a sensitivity band across candidate Kd from 1.8 nM to 12 µM, or dropped — and the revision took the second. `sensitivity.svg` remains a kinetics figure (t_off against assumed kon, with the orange band labeled as non-glutamate Ding endpoints), not a θ sensitivity band, so the band was not built; that is within the named options.
+
+One residual item belongs here rather than under any figure. `state/model_disagreements.md` and `analysis/accepted/occupancy_kinetics/limitations.md` both disclose that the accepted analysis locks the overlay arithmetic in a test named `test_hu_saturated_at_tonic`. The arithmetic is true as overlay math and both files say so, but the test's *name* asserts the withdrawn finding, and a test name is the one label that survives every refactor and gets read by the next agent as a statement of fact. It should be renamed to describe what it locks — overlay θ at Herman's ambient on an advertised Kd — because as written it is a latent re-entry point for the claim this mission withdrew.
+
+## Fatal defect
+
+**I identify none.** The candidate fatal defect for this closure was the one the instructions name: that the withdrawn occupancy claim might be smuggled back through the storyboard or the figures. It is not. The flagship draws no 1.8 nM glyph; Panel 4's claim is the UNKNOWN itself, with 1.8 nM parked in an explicitly different-device, different-isotherm well; Probe 3 appears only as author-flagged failure analysis with the occupancy reading `unresolved`; and the Must-not-claim list names θ(25 nM)≈0.93-as-tissue-occupancy, 1.8 nM-as-the-retinal-probe's-molecular-Kd, koff ≈ 1/1.2 ms, extrasynaptic-only 25 nM, 0.3 pM as an Ames or tissue LOD, in vivo glutamate aptamer sensing, and the unentered Abrantes millimolar ELONA Kd. I also checked the revision against the hash-locked safety file specifically: every number in the canonical thesis traces to a ledger row or is arithmetic on ledger rows, the 39-mer length matches the sequence in E036, no citation or identifier is invented, no full-text inspection is claimed where the ledger records otherwise, and both the poster-freeze and human-approval rules are honored on the face of the documents ("Not a finished poster. Not group-final.").
+
+## Whether quantity types, devices and matrices remain distinct
+
+Yes, with named exceptions. The distinctions that matter are carried throughout: Hu's 12 µM is typed as a *citation* of Wu in the methods rather than a Hu remeasurement (C021), and is kept apart from the 1.8 nM apparent electrochemical `EC50` on the same chip; 1.8 nM is kept apart from Herman's 1.8 µM NMDAR EC50 on nucleated patches (E035) with the digit collision named; 32 and 51.5 pM stay AuED-MEA LODs; 0.3 pM is printed with its estimator (blank + 3 RSD), its matrix (PBS, not Ames) and its calibration floor (lowest calibrant 1 nM), which is exactly what the prior review demanded and is the single best hygiene improvement in the package; Xiao's 293 nM SPR Kd and 10 fM FET LOD in 0.1× PBS stay separate quantities in a named buffer; and the empty glutamate kon/koff cell stays empty, with tobramycin and Ding explicitly non-transferable.
+
+Three exceptions. The clearest is in the thesis's retired-title-C bullet: "Hu 32 pM is a real matrix-matched LOD." 32 pM is the PBS LOD (C004/E005); the matrix-matched number is 51.5 pM in 50% serum (E006). The phrasing is inherited from the prior review's own wording, it sits on a supporting panel rather than on a load-bearing row, and it is a matrix mislabel of exactly the class this gate polices. Second, the thesis prints 0.3 pM's estimator and calibration floor but not 32 pM's (blank + 3 SD on a fit whose lowest calibrant is 0.1 nM, roughly threefold of extrapolation), so the 3 SD / 3 RSD asymmetry the prior review flagged is half-closed. Third, the Panel 5 duplication noted above weakens the very key that is supposed to prevent collapse. I also note, without reading it, that `atlas.svg` is un-inspected here, so I cannot certify that Panel 5's glyph matches its text.
+
+## Whether any glyph still implies measured tissue occupancy from 1.8 nM
+
+No glyph implies *measured* tissue occupancy. In the flagship I confirmed by coordinate scan that no element is drawn at the 1.8 nM position; the number appears only as body text stating that it is an AuED-MEA PBS Langmuir–Freundlich apparent Kd and is *not* drawn as tissue occupancy or as the retinal probe's molecular Kd, and the panel carries a hard-bordered UNKNOWN box reading "PaC probe θ in Ames/tissue — unmeasured". `two_regime_clocks.svg` contains no occupancy glyph and no 1.8 nM.
+
+`occupancy.svg` still renders the θ curve generated from 1.8 nM, and that curve still passes through 0.93 at the 25 nM line — I read it off the polyline (y≈70.06 on a 350-to-50 axis). What has changed is that the figure now argues against its own reading on its own canvas: the title line reads "DEMOTED 1:1 overlay SIMULATION — advertised Kd/EC50, not tissue occupancy, not PaC Kd", it carries a MODELED stamp, the legend entry names the device and isotherm class ("AuED-MEA LF 1.8 nM (not PaC)"), "PaC θ UNKNOWN" is printed inside the plot, and the footer restates device, isotherm and matrix. The storyboard permits it only as a supporting inset and forbids it as Panel 4's claim. That is sufficient, but it is sufficient *because* of the demotion, so the demotion has to hold in production: if this figure is ever enlarged to flagship scale the 0.93 reading returns, and its overlapping tick labels make it the weakest figure in the set. The one place the withdrawn claim still survives in asserted form is not a glyph and not the storyboard — it is the `test_hu_saturated_at_tonic` test name.
+
+## Whether biological-context transfers are explicit
+
+Yes, and this is the most improved dimension of the package. The Herman-to-retina and Clements-to-retina transfers are refused in the thesis one-sentence form ("two commonly cited hippocampal literature concentrations"), in the full statement ("literature examples from different hippocampal experimental contexts… not a measured retinal concentration range, not a specification for Hu's parylene-C probe, and not a license to treat retina as a failed hippocampal-cleft sensor"), in load-bearing row 3 with `transferable` marked unknown, in the three-way Measured / Inferred / Unknown inference boundary, in the Must-not-claim list, in Panel 1, on the canvas of both flagship figures, and in the accepted-analysis caption. Herman is labeled as acute hippocampal slice with the "extrasynaptic-only" reading refused, which matches the citation audit's finding that the word appears in Herman only inside a citation. Clements is labeled a kinetic inference at cultured hippocampal synapses, abstract-only, and a *different preparation* from Herman's slices — that preparation distinction is new and is the sharper half of the fix. Device and matrix transfers are equally explicit: AuED-MEA to parylene-C probe blocked, PBS to Ames to tissue blocked with the Ames window and poor SNR recorded, Wu's 1d04 to glu1 blocked, tobramycin and Ding rates blocked, and the enzyme and genetically-encoded sensors kept as labeled comparators.
+
+One transfer-blocking statement is itself unsourced. "Photoreceptor glutamate is graded, not Clements-quantal" appears in both the thesis and Panel 1 with no claim row and no tag. It is used defensively, to prevent a transfer rather than to support a finding, and it introduces no number, so it does not touch the never-invent rule. But an untagged biological assertion on a panel is still an untagged assertion, and it should either get a `review-supported` source or be restated in the conservative form that needs none: Clements' quantal-cleft preparation is not evidence about photoreceptor release.
+
+## Consolidated residual defects
+
+For the record, the complete list of what I found, none of which requires a change to the thesis text, to either flagship figure's content, or to any claim's evidential grade: promote the Probes 1–2 light-correlated ACV outcome into `claims.csv` with the E046 locator, tag and `full_text_inspected` before printing its MEASURED stamp; promote the GCL/IPL-border electrode location rather than citing sealed lane notes; promote or drop the dopamine 49.6-versus-cited-44 µM near-match, which is printed in a supporting bullet but has no row in either ledger; source or soften the photoreceptor-graded-release sentence; rename `test_hu_saturated_at_tonic`; correct "32 pM is a real matrix-matched LOD" to name PBS, with 51.5 pM as the matrix-matched value; fix Panel 5's duplicated 10 fM and restore Wu's 0.0013 pM; fix the overlapping tick labels in `occupancy.svg`; print the authors' 41.6% Ames blank-noise caveat on Panel 3 where the positive claim is made; and give both flagship figures a real labeled axis carrying unit and quantity type.
+
+## Overall gate recommendation
+
+**PASS**, on the existing five criteria and without weakening any of them. The gate previously failed on one hard "no" and one "partial", and both have been repaired in the canonical artifacts rather than in commentary: occupancy-at-basal is withdrawn as a finding and stamped unmeasured in the thesis, the storyboard, and the flagship figure; Probe 3 is demoted to author-flagged gold-detachment failure with the occupancy reading unresolved; the electrode-layer tension is printed on-panel as an open question; the θ=0.93 overlay is off the flagship, and the flagship that replaced it is an exact 81-fold identity against an exact 44,000-fold literature span that I verified from the figure's own coordinates and that admits no aptamer number, so the computation is the argument rather than an illustration hung beside it. The withdrawal is not a relabeling and it is not smuggled back: the remaining load-bearing claims are inspected primary evidence, correctly graded algebra, or honestly empty cells, and the two abstract-only items have had their assertion levels lowered to what their abstracts support rather than their sources promoted. I record that revised D is a materially weaker *claim* than the one submitted — its strength now lies in framing, in a Kd-free identity, and in two refusals it was entitled to make — and that the criterion-1 margin rests on structure rather than on any post-revision score, since none exists and I have not supplied one. The defects I found are real and must be closed before anything is printed, but they are ledger promotions, one test rename, and figure labeling, and not one of them reinstates the withdrawn occupancy finding or changes a claim's grade; a reader whose convention is that any required change forces REVISE should treat the consolidated list above as the complete set. I identify no fatal defect.
